Fix: tools/ladder/musl_case.py uses the upstream RUN_WRAP mechanism in both
reference and candidate trials. Only the two exact atfork test paths drop root
to uid/gid 65534 with supplementary groups cleared. All other cases keep their
identity. Setup errors fail; no assertion or result is suppressed. Four actual
installed-wrapper executions (two variants x two archives) PASS under the
unchanged supervisor. Unit tests cover path boundaries, already-nonroot users,
and failed privilege drop. The adapter records the wrapper hash and policy.

Assembler REDs: omitted -Xassembler, lost ordering/argument boundaries, and
acceptance of partial stdout after failed container execution. Fixed using
ordered flag extraction and an exact JSON argv plan. Five regression tests pass,
including executing the generated runner with literal spaces and shell text.
Six native ELF objects pass: -Wa/--noexecstack and -Xassembler/--noexecstack
produce non-executable GNU-stack notes; --execstack produces X; mixed-spelling
last override wins in both orders; --defsym guard=37 appears as absolute 0x25.
The historical -Wa,--noexecstack spelling already worked; do not claim it was
previously ignored just because the C frontend omission table named it.

